/*
 * XorWoW TCG: a card game between two players, played on a 3x3 board drawn by the XorWoW addon.
 * The server is the referee: it owns every account's cards, deck and record, checks the challenges,
 * plays the rules and moves the cards bet between the players. The addon only draws and sends moves.
 *
 * Cards: the world table xorwow_tcg_card (generated by scripts\client-patch\build_tcg.py); card N
 * drops as item 261000+N, whose use spell (261000) adds it to the account's collection. A card
 * counts once its expansion is open (the level cap: 60 classic, 70 +tbc, 80 +wotlk).
 *
 * Rules (FF8's Triple Triad rules, renamed): each player plays the 5 cards of the deck saved in
 * the collection window, one card per turn on an empty square. A side higher than the touching
 * side of an enemy card flips it. Always on: Combo (with Same or Plus) and
 * Elemental: 1-3 random squares carry an element, a card of that element gets +1 on every side
 * there, a card of another element -1, a card without one nothing; and a card whose element beats
 * the other's on the circle (Water > Fire > Frost > Earth > Arcane > Holy > Shadow > Nature >
 * Water) gets +1 on the touching side for that comparison. Same and Plus use the printed numbers.
 * Set by the challenger: Open (both hands shown, else the opponent's cards stay face down until
 * played), Same and Plus (all three on by default), Same Wall (the board's edges count as A for
 * Same) and Sudden Death (a draw is replayed, up to 3 times, with the cards each player holds).
 * Stakes, agreed before the game: none, One (the winner takes 1 card of the loser's deck) or Diff
 * (as many as the score difference). A deck is 5 different owned cards, at most one of tier 9-10
 * and at most two of tier 7 or more; a valid deck is needed to challenge and to accept.
 *
 * A player who leaves duel range, dies, teleports, changes zone or logs out during a game loses it
 * (counted as "fled" in the record) and the winner still takes the stakes.
 *
 * Bots: the world's bots (not the alts played by the bot AI) take any challenge at once. The server
 * plays for them: each bot has a strategy for good (Bad, Poor, Medium, Strong, Perfect, table
 * xorwow_tcg_bot, rolled once per bot character) that sets how often it plays a move other than the
 * best one it found, and it builds a deck from every open card whose tiers add up as close as
 * possible to the challenger's deck. Bots never see a face-down hand. Bot games have no stakes, do not
 * count for the achievements and keep their own record and history (the stats' Bots tab).
 *
 * A win (at the board or by the other one leaving) gives WIN_XP experience, or at the level cap
 * its worth in money the way quests convert it (6 copper per point).
 *
 * Achievements: the "XorWoW TCG" category of the achievement window (rows from
 * scripts\client-patch\gen_tcg_achievements.py). Each criteria waits on a spell nobody casts
 * (type 28, spell 269000 + Stat); its count is kept here per account (the record, the streak, the
 * collection and one bit per feat) and set on the character playing, so every character of the
 * account earns them, at the latest when its addon says hello.
 *
 * Protocol: addon messages, prefix "XorWoW", body "TCG;<command>;...", whispered by the addon to
 * its own player and swallowed here; the answers are addon whispers to the player. The chat hook,
 * the logout and death hooks and the card spell only queue events: everything is done in the
 * world update, on the world thread, so the game state has one owner.
 */

